{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pulls/11","id":4900838093,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVMrF8s8AAAABJBzazQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/11","diff_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/11.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/11.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/issues/11","number":11,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Protect report inputs and retained evidence during output preflight","user":{"login":"tsm0420","id":62269874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMjY5ODc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62269874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420","html_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nA configured input placed at a report filename could be overwritten with exit 0. A later invalid destination could also replace JSON before failing, leaving it inconsistent with retained raw evidence. Report commands now protect input identities and preflight the complete destination set before writing.\n\n```text\ninputs + destination identities -> full preflight -> write JSON / Markdown / evidence\n                         conflict -> exit 2, original bytes retained\n```\n\nThis is deterministic preflight, with explicit disk/power/concurrent-path limits, rather than transactional rollback. Relates to #10 (TICKET-009 only; other slices remain planned). **Depends on unmerged #9**; this PR targets its branch.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal CLI red/green tests reproduce direct/hard-link input overwrites, mutually aliased outputs and predictable late conflicts. Final focused tests: 15 pass; full suite: 48 pass, no skips; typecheck/build pass. Independent Standards and Spec reports have no actionable introduced defects.\n\nReviewed source: `ec2b23caf57e22f106da7b07bb37f1b344e08981`. A clean archive and extracted alpha.3 package passed all 16 expected command outcomes, including all six commands and original-byte preservation. Frozen YinThread remains 16 pass / 1 fail / 2 unknown, 146 entries / 145 unique, duplicate positions 8,12. Package SHA-256: `93ed2264bccbc5854f9dc4ed105ca8b3167f84dee43d407bcb76e0a5313761b0`.\n\nRaw commands/exits/runtime/inventory: `docs/verification/TICKET-009/`; separate reviews: `docs/reviews/TICKET-009/`. Current head `79a7edbbe201ebd1e63d14d10e126ebdeff051f9` adds evidence/docs only; executable and packaged inputs are unchanged. Exact-head CI succeeded for `79a7edbbe201ebd1e63d14d10e126ebdeff051f9`: [verify job](https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/actions/runs/39040390851/job/117418524995), observed through Code Review. The Ubuntu 24.04.5 x64 / Node v24.21.0 job passed 48 tests, typecheck/build and fictional report generation. No tagged release is inferred.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\nDoor: two-way. Blast radius: local report output preflight across audit/aso/plan/visibility. Intended new errors reject unsafe destinations before writes. Init/install and successful output reuse are preserved. No new dependencies, merge, tag, release, live crawl or publication.","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:21:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T14:22:13Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2aa1eaf705ed7d2ea109facd6dd09b54c7089ee7","assignees":[],"requested